  "comments": "<p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><br>Two main groups of the reverse are known.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><i>Reverse</i><br>Die <strong>A</strong> - Kalevala's ornament to the left of denomination \"5\" close to it.<br>Die <strong>B</strong> - Kalevala's ornament to the left of denomination \"5\" far from it.</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>A</strong>: 1952 (see main photos of the article), 1953.<br><strong>B</strong>: 1953. Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer ugc\" href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6602910437d08.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6602910437d08.jpg\"></a></p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/660aad793638a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/660aad793638a.jpg\"></a></p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><i>Note</i>. Die <strong>B</strong> was in use during the next emission struck on nickel plated iron blanks till 1962.</p>",
